# Project Description and Basics

## Description

This is a WordPress website for the ART/New York organization. The site customizations currently consist of a custom theme, `rhd-art-new-york`.

## Xplor integration
API Documentation for the Xplor integration is here: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1X8HgElUwBL-KHQG1eClP919hsWjlWrXx/view

## Xplor API access
PERFECTMIND_BASE_URL, PERFECTMIND_API_KEY, PERFECTMIND_CLIENT_NUMBER are all defined constants.

- PERFECTMIN_BASE_URL is the remote Xplor server to query.
- PERFECTMIND_REST_BASE is the REST endpoint base to query.
- PERFECTMIND_API_KEY is sent in each REST operation as the X-Access-Key header.
- PERFECTMIND_CLIENT_NUMBER is sent in each REST operation as the X-Client-Number header.

## RHD block plugins (e.g. `rhd-artny-directory`)

- Follow the pattern in `wp-content/plugins/rhd-cover-parallax-block` and `wp-content/plugins/rhd-artny-directory`: `block.json` + `render.php`, Roundhouse naming (`rhd-*`), theme-aligned markup using `wp-block-*` classes and `theme.json` CSS variables.
- **Dynamic blocks must register in the editor client-side (WP 7+).** Server-only `register_block_type()` is not enough — the editor will show “Your site doesn't include support for the block.” Register `assets/editor.js` explicitly in PHP with dependencies: `wp-blocks`, `wp-element`, `wp-block-editor`, `wp-server-side-render`, `wp-components`. Do not rely on `block.json` `"editorScript": "file:./…"` alone; auto-registered editor scripts may load with **empty deps** and fail silently.
- **Editor registration:** `unregisterBlockType` then `registerBlockType` when a `block.json` block needs a custom `edit` with `ServerSideRender`. A `getBlockType()` early-return guard alone can leave bootstrapped blocks without a working `edit` callback.
- **ServerSideRender attributes:** The block-renderer REST endpoint validates attributes with `additionalProperties: false`. Only pass attributes declared in that block’s `block.json` (typically `align` and other registered keys). Do **not** pass full `props.attributes` or client-only keys (e.g. a `directoryType` not in `block.json`) — this yields `Error loading block: Invalid parameter(s): attributes`. Prefer resolving behavior from the registered block name when variants share render code.
- **Block alignment:** When `supports.align` is enabled, apply alignment only via the block `align` attribute (e.g. `alignwide` / `alignfull` classes from `$attributes['align']`). Do **not** hardcode `alignfull` or `alignwide` on the block wrapper — that overrides the editor control.
- Use `ServerSideRender` in `edit` for editor preview of dynamic blocks.
- **Render core block output via `do_blocks()` or `render_block()`** — do not hand-roll markup for blocks that ship icons/assets (e.g. `core/social-links` needs SVG icons from core). Match demo page block attributes (icon colors, layout) when mirroring existing designs.
- **Multiple block variants:** Prefer separate registered block names (e.g. Organizations vs Individuals) with distinct inserter titles. Share PHP/JS/CSS via config — do not register duplicate or legacy block names in the inserter unless content migration requires it; use `supports.inserter: false` or omit legacy registration entirely when backwards compatibility is not needed.
- **Front-end block asset versions:** For shared plugin `view.js` / `style.css` assets on live pages, register handles in PHP with `filemtime()` versions instead of relying on static `block.json` versions. CDN/browser caches can keep serving stale `?ver=1.0.0` assets even when disk files and containers are updated.
- When renaming a plugin: rename folder + main file, update all slugs/classes/text domains/block names, swap `active_plugins` entry, and update `<!-- wp:namespace/block -->` comments in post content.
- Verify on dev: plugin active, block registered after `init`, page renders expected markup (`docker exec … php -r "require wp-load.php; …"`), and the browser is loading the expected asset URLs/content (query string and fetched JS/CSS source), not a cached CDN copy. For editor issues, also verify REST block-renderer accepts the attributes `ServerSideRender` sends.

## UI details in directory cards

- `<details><summary>` defaults to bold in browsers — set `font-weight: 400` (or `normal`) explicitly when summary should match body text.
- Scope card typography overrides under plugin classes (e.g. `.rhd-artny-directory__card .wp-block-details`) using theme font-size presets (`--wp--preset--font-size--small`).
- **`[hidden]` vs CSS `display`:** Any rule that sets `display` (e.g. flex/grid) on a control that toggles the HTML `hidden` attribute must also define the matching `[hidden] { display: none !important; }` (see `.rhd-artny-directory__pagination` and cards). Otherwise Prev/Next (or similar) stays visible on single-page result sets even when JS sets `hidden`.

## Directory filter form layout (`rhd-artny-directory`)

- **Peer wrapping, not nested side-by-side:** Search and each filter dropdown must be peers in one `auto-fit` / `minmax` grid so they wrap together across breakpoints. Use `display: contents` on `__filter-groups` so dropdowns participate in the form grid. Do **not** put search in column 1 and a nested wrapping filter grid in column 2.
- **Avoid `align-items: end` on wrapping filter bars:** That alignment looks correct when all fields share one row (inputs line up), but when filters wrap to multiple rows the short search cell sinks to the last row. Prefer `align-items: start`.
- **Shared stylesheet:** Organizations and Individuals share `assets/style.css` — fix layout once; both variants inherit it.
- **No public layout fixtures:** Do not leave repro/test HTML under plugin `assets/` (it is served). Use `/tmp` or a non-web path for CSS layout probes; prefer static CSS contract checks when headless browsers are unavailable.

## Accessible multi-select filter dropdowns

When replacing checkbox groups with compact multi-select filters (directory block and similar RHD UI):

- **Pattern:** disclosure button + panel of checkboxes — not `<select multiple>` (modifier keys) and not listbox without full ARIA support.
- **Markup:** visible group label (`id` on label span) → `.filter-dropdown-control` wrapper (positioned) → `type="button"` trigger + `hidden` panel with checkboxes. Keep existing `data-*-filter` attributes on inputs so client-side `readFilters()` stays unchanged.
- **Trigger ARIA:** `aria-labelledby="{label-id} {summary-id}"` so the accessible name includes **both** the group name and current selection. Give the summary span its own `id`; update its `textContent` in JS. Use disclosure pattern: `aria-expanded` + `aria-controls` pointing at the panel (keep the panel in the DOM with `hidden` when closed). Do **not** use `aria-haspopup` on these triggers — with `hidden` panels, scanners flag `aria-controls` as unresolved (`aria-valid-attr-value`), and APG disclosures do not require haspopup. Do **not** put `aria-live` inside the button — it fights `aria-labelledby` and causes duplicate announcements.
- **Panel ARIA:** `role="group"` + `aria-labelledby` on the group label only. Avoid redundant `<fieldset>`/`<legend>` inside the panel when the group is already labeled.
- **Keyboard / behavior:** Enter/Space opens; Escape closes and returns focus to trigger; click outside closes; only one panel open at a time. Checkboxes must not be in tab order when panel is `hidden`.
- **Status / empty states:** Result counts and **zero-result messages** must go through an existing `role="status" aria-live="polite"` region. Do not clear the live region and rely on a separate static empty element alone. If a visible empty message remains for sighted users, mark it `aria-hidden="true"` when the live region carries the announcement.
- **Visible filter summaries vs live regions:** If adding a visible “Filtered by …” summary, keep visible text and `role="status"` count text from duplicating each other. Use a separate visually hidden span inside the live region only when extra context needs to be announced to screen readers.
- **Helper copy:** Associate instructional text with the form via `aria-describedby`.
- **Verification:** Do not treat accessible UI as complete from markup/implementation alone. Run structured verification (live page DOM, keyboard paths, accessible names) before sign-off; fix Major WCAG gaps (4.1.2 Name/Role/Value, 4.1.3 Status Messages) before claiming AA-ready.

## Directory block data and filters (`rhd-artny-directory`)

- **Config-driven variants:** Use a central config (table, fields, taxonomies, eligibility, block name) for each directory type. Share API, cache, render, and `view.js`; resolve variant from block name in render — avoid duplicating block plugins.
- **Eligibility vs filter options:** Displayable cards and filter dropdowns are not the same dataset. A sync may have zero displayable contacts (e.g. missing bio/web presence) while taxonomy labels still exist from raw API rows. Populate filter dropdowns from cached taxonomy labels when no displayable contact carries that slug; do not hide filters solely because `contacts` is empty.
- **Cache:** Use the cached payload when present even if `contacts` is empty, so labels and sync metadata persist between requests. Bump the type’s `cache_key` when transform, eligibility, field-resolution precedence, or normalized contact shape changes (e.g. adding Xplor `ID` onto contacts).
- **Xplor record identity:** Keep Account/Contact `ID` through API normalize → transform → cached contacts whenever features need a stable key (manual exclusions, admin tooling). Do not render `ID` on public cards. Demo fallback contacts need stable demo IDs too.
- **Xplor Contact vs Account:** Individuals use `Contact` (name from `FirstName`/`MiddleName`/`LastName`, `PrimaryPractice`, `ArtisticPractices`, individual social fields). Organizations use `Account` (`AccountType = Organization`). Keep separate cache keys and cron hooks per type.
- **Organizations field roles (do not conflate):**
  - Questionnaire / profile data for orgs lives on the Account’s `PrimaryContact` (Contact row). Prefer PrimaryContact values when non-empty; fall back to the matching Account field. Do not treat Account and Contact org fields as interchangeable sources without an explicit precedence rule.
  - `OrganizationBio` (PrimaryContact) → preferred card About/`Description`. Account `Description` → fallback only when primary contact has no `OrganizationBio`.
  - Website → PrimaryContact `OrganizationWebsiteforProfile`, else Account `Website`, else Account `WebsiteforProfile`.
  - Instagram → PrimaryContact `OrganizationInstagram`, else Account `Instagram`.
  - LinkedIn → PrimaryContact `OrganizationLinkedInProfile`, else Account `OrganizationLinkedInProfile` / `LinkedInProfileURL`.
  - Facebook → PrimaryContact `OrganizationFacebookPage`, else Account `OrganizationFacebookPage`.
  - Taxonomies (`ArtisticFocus`, `OrganizationalFocus`, `PublicProgrammingLocations`) → same field names on Contact and Account; prefer PrimaryContact when `parse_multi_value` yields labels, else Account.
  - Fetch all PrimaryContact-sourced org fields (`MembershipExpiry`, `OrganizationBio`, website/social/taxonomy keys above) via a single `fetch_primary_contact_map()` Contact table fetch; do not add a second Contact query per field.
  - Normalized `Description` satisfies `require_description` eligibility when present.
- **Org field remap inventory:** Before changing Account→PrimaryContact mappings, list each field by role: displayed, keyword-searchable (`data-search`), filter-dropdown, and eligibility-only. Keep card/render normalized keys stable; change resolution in the transform layer and bump the org `cache_key`.
- **Individuals field roles (do not conflate):**
  - `ArtistBio` → card About/`Description` content only (map when `Description` empty). Not a display gate unless `require_description` is true.
  - `PrimaryPractice` → questionnaire-completed signal; used when `require_web_presence` is false as an alternate eligibility path.
  - Web/social (`IndividualMemberWebsite`, Instagram, Facebook, LinkedIn) → default display gate when `require_web_presence` is true (organizations always require web presence).
  - “Require bio” always means the **eligibility gate** (`require_description`), not merely showing About when a bio exists. If the user’s intent is ambiguous after a temporary relaxation, confirm before flipping.
- **Temporary eligibility relaxations:** Prefer explicit config flags (`require_description`, `require_web_presence`) with comments and a cache-key bump—not silent hardcoding. Restore stricter flags when questionnaire completion is healthy.
- **Before flipping eligibility flags:** Measure and report the projected before/after displayable count (and who drops) **before** declaring success. A sudden drop after tightening a gate (e.g. bio required → 6 to 2) is usually expected, not a sync bug—show the excluded names so the user can confirm intent.
- **Individuals bio field:** Questionnaire bios live in `ArtistBio`, not `Description`. Map `ArtistBio` into the card `Description` when `Description` is empty. Include `ArtistBio` (and `Email` when filtering) in Contact field picks.
- **Individuals test contacts:** Exclude Contact emails whose local part contains `+test` (Xplor questionnaire test accounts). Do not treat repeated names or mismatched websites/bios as a transform bug until raw ObjectRecords rows are checked — CRM test pollution often explains both.
- **Directory data debugging:** When cards look wrong or too few, measure the eligibility funnel on raw ObjectRecords (named → not test → not expired → has PrimaryPractice → has ArtistBio → has web) before changing rules. Sparse displayable counts with many active memberships usually mean incomplete questionnaire/web presence, not a render bug.
- **Directory transform verification:** When changing field mapping or precedence, define the both-fields-populated case before implementing empty-only fallbacks. Verify with `docker exec … php -r "require wp-load.php; …"`: precedence regression, `refresh_cache()`, counts of records with both source fields, and an individuals smoke-check when org transform changes.
- **Membership expiry:** Exclude expired entries from directory cards after `MEMBERSHIP_EXPIRY_GRACE_DAYS` (60) past the expiry date. Organizations: resolve `PrimaryContact` to a Contact `ID` and apply that contact's `MembershipExpiry`; exclude orgs with no primary contact, missing contact map, or absent/expired primary contact membership (null/empty/sentinel expiry = expired). Individuals: skip when `MembershipExpiry` is explicitly past the grace window; null/empty/sentinel expiry does not alone exclude an individual. Bump cache keys when eligibility rules change.
- **Manual ineligible exclusions:** Staff can force-remove members immediately (including during the grace window) via Settings → Directory exclusions. Store Xplor IDs in option `rhd_artny_directory_ineligible` with a name snapshot (`name` + `updated_at`) so flagged rows remain manageable after they leave the public cache. Skip ineligible IDs in org/individual transform **before** membership/grace checks; also filter in `get_contacts()` so a stale cache cannot keep showing them; refresh that type’s cache on admin save. Do not rely on an Xplor CRM field for this.
- **Filtered exclusion admin saves:** The exclusions UI supports name search. Never rebuild the type’s exclusion map from only POSTed checked boxes on a filtered view—that wipes IDs not rendered. Post `visible_ids[]` for every rendered row, merge: drop visible-but-unchecked IDs, add/update checked IDs, leave non-visible existing exclusions untouched.
